{
  "note": "Phase-1 parity cases for `lucina parity`: every /api/secretary route secretary-server uses, chat turns in it/en/da, shopping v1/v2, reminders, agenda, timeline + SSE, notes, calendar, outfit, presence, MCP turns (allowed and refused), jobs. Synthetic messages only. `allow` lists response paths whose difference is expected; `why` says why.",
  "textAllow": [
    "Offers on your shopping list",
    "Nothing on your shopping list is on offer",
    "Your shopping list is empty, so I have nothing to match offers against",
    "Live grocery catalog lookup is not configured yet.",
    "graph task failed:"
  ],
  "textAllowWhy": "The two expected divergences (no catalog/offer adapters in Rust yet; graph_task stays with Node) also show up in timeline listings, SSE replays and the appended timeline lines.",
